{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Great is my punishment to bear.</b> The punishment of my iniquity that You laid upon me — I cannot bear it, for You have banished me, etc. <b>My punishment</b> — as in 'the punishment of the daughter of my people is greater than the sin of Sodom,' 'if my punishment touches you in this matter.' Another interpretation: <b>Great is my punishment to bear</b> — in astonishment: You have banished me by causing the earth no longer to give its strength to me. My father sinned against You and was banished from the Garden of Eden, and it was atoned for him; but me, whom You banished to be a wanderer and fugitive — You should have atoned for me."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:55.054782451Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}